.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.TH batten-state 1  batten 
.SH NAME
batten\-state \- The out\-of\-tree findings store: which store belongs to this checkout
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBbatten state\fR [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fIsubcommands\fR>
.SH DESCRIPTION
The out\-of\-tree findings store: which store belongs to this checkout
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.SH SUBCOMMANDS
.TP
batten\-state\-adopt(1)
Bind this checkout to its findings store, minting one only if none exists
.TP
batten\-state\-record(1)
Record this ref\*(Aqs findings into the store, and GC instances whose ref is gone
.TP
batten\-state\-migrate(1)
Upgrade the findings store to this binary\*(Aqs record version
.TP
batten\-state\-list(1)
List stored findings and the refs they were observed in
.TP
batten\-state\-help(1)
Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)
